course: dictionary
lesson: 29
title: Abstract words and ideas
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Some words name things you can touch, like a mat or a dog. Others name ideas and feelings you cannot touch. «A concrete noun names something you can see or touch, like a mat; an abstract noun names an idea or feeling, like happiness, fear or friendship.» Happiness is not a thing on a shelf, so it is abstract.
explain: Ask yourself: could I put this in a box or point to it? If not, it is probably abstract. Love, fairness and time are abstract. Try your idea in a sentence: «Fairness matters to me.» You can think about fairness, but you cannot hold it.
explain: Abstract has other meanings too. In art, «abstract art» uses shapes and colours instead of real things. In a science report, the abstract is a short summary at the start. Check the sentence around the word to see which meaning it has.
fact: Abstract means an idea or feeling rather than a thing you can touch or see.
fact: Love, fairness and time are abstract ideas.
fact: Abstract art uses shapes, colours and lines, not real things.
fact: A concrete noun names something you can touch, like a mat.
fact: The abstract of a science report is a short summary at its start.
exercise: «Abstract art does not show recognisable things.» What does abstract art use instead? | Photographs of places | *Shapes and colours | Long stories | Real animals and people
exercise: Which word is an abstract noun? | Mat | *Friendship | Dog | Table
exercise: In maths, why are numbers called abstract? | Because they are the same as shapes | Because they are always written in red | *Because a number like three is an idea, not a thing | Because they are made of wood
test: What is an abstract noun? | A word for a place, like school | A word for an action, like run | A word for a thing you can touch | *A word for an idea or feeling, like fear
test: In science, what does the abstract of a report tell you? | The name of the author's dog | Pictures of the experiment | A list of jokes | *A short summary of what was found
exam: Freedom and love are abstract. What does abstract mean here? | To take something out | *An idea or feeling, not a thing you can touch | A short summary at the start | A painting with bright colours
